// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_landing_late.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: check_landings' LATE edge — a burst that is still writing when the next
//          scanline is sampled (substrate item 1c).
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "past the latest legal"
//
// Register writes and then a 3-word pal_region. The burst arrives so late that the
// solver has nothing left to spend: it clamps to zero iterations and check_landings
// reports the landing it could not place, naming the op index, the fire line, the
// computed cycle and the window edge.
//
// RE-DERIVED FOR TIER-3 ITEM 2, AND THE RE-DERIVATION IS ITSELF THE FINDING. This case
// used to be `fire(100, [reg, reg, reg, stream_cram 1w])` — four ops, exactly the
// per-fire ceiling, every other guard satisfied. It worked because each OP_SET_REG cost
// 110 cycles, so three of them put the cram's delay site 330 cycles into the record and
// past the window before it had spun at all. Item 2 cut a register write to 40 cycles,
// and at 40 THE OLD SHAPE IS LEGAL: the cram now reaches its site at 190 modelled
// cycles, the solver gives it 9 iterations, and it lands centred.
//
// That is not a hole; it is the parcel working. But it does mean NO SHAPE `fire()` WILL
// BUILD CAN STILL REACH THE LATE EDGE, and the arithmetic says so exhaustively. Late-only
// needs the solved spin clamped to 0 with the first write still inside the early edge,
// i.e. p >= 234.1 and p + 14 + span > 341. Over every legal fire:
//   * two stream ops in one fire always trip the EARLY edge first (their combined span is
//     at least 124 cycles, so the solver's centre lands the first write at 227.6 or
//     lower) — a two-diagnostic case, not this one;
//   * one stream op behind the most register writes the four-op ceiling allows tops out
//     at p = 3 x 40 + 8 + 42 + 56 = 226 for the deepest non-restore op (pal_region), and
//     226 solves to 2 iterations and lands its last word at 320, inside the 341 edge;
//   * a pal_restore is deep enough (p = 274 with three regs ahead), but D-B refuses any
//     fire that carries a restore plus anything else, so that shape reports D-B — and the
//     band-pairing walk besides — rather than this.
//
// SO THIS POISON NOW DODGES THE CEILING THE WAY poison_direct_8a DODGES reg_set's own
// ensure: `RasterFire.Fire(line, ops)` is the variant `fire()` returns, constructed
// directly, so the four-op ceiling never runs. That is a legitimate poison and not a
// cheat — raster_program's $0A/$0F ban-scan exists precisely because a constructor-only
// refusal is not a refusal, and the same reasoning applies to a landing guard: it must
// still fire on the op list it is handed, whatever built it. FIVE register writes put the
// region's delay site at p = 5 x 40 + 8 + 42 + 56 = 306, the solver clamps to 0, the first
// write lands at 320 (inside the early edge, which is 248.1) and the last at 380 — 39
// cycles past the latest legal 341.
//
// EXACTLY ONE DIAGNOSTIC. The EARLY edge passes (the burst is late, not early — 320 is
// comfortably past 248.1) and the five register ops carry no burst at all, so a count of 2
// here would mean a second guard started firing and this poison stopped naming one thing.
// In particular it must NOT be the per-fire ceiling: if that appears, the direct
// construction above has stopped dodging it and this case is testing the wrong guard.
//
// NO IMPORTS, like every ordinary author's module: raster_dsl and engine.vdp are
// COMPTIME_HELPERS members, glob-injected into every module by the real build. See
// the README on why the lane cannot reproduce that injection yet.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_landing_late

const POISON_LANDING_LATE = [
    RasterFire.Fire(100, [reg_set($8C81), reg_set($8C81), reg_set($8C81), reg_set($8C81),
                          reg_set($8C81), stream_pal_region($22, 0, 1, 1, 3)]),
]

// THE ELABORATION HOOK — see poison_two_restores.emp's note. Trivially-true predicate;
// the diagnostic under test comes from inside the call.
ensure(raster_program(POISON_LANDING_LATE).len > 0,
       "poison_landing_late: raster_program returned nothing — this poison no longer reaches the guard it targets")
